{"ts":"2026-09-28T23:02:04.624Z","type":"spawn.report","run":"run-20260928-191959","spec":"harness-control-pane","agent":"sdd-drafter","report":"I wrote tasks v1 for harness-control-pane and sent the hand-off report to the orchestrator. It has 20 tasks covering design components C1-C10, the data models and the testing strategy, and every task is under the 150-word cap. Nothing is committed.\n\n- **Launch race loser:** it now gets a 409 with no run id. A second launch is refused while one is starting, and the route checks, writes the setup file and starts the launch in one step so two requests can't slip past together. The launcher also rejects a second launch itself, with a new `admission` error step; only worktree, setup and spawn failures give a 500 (decision D1, tasks 5 and 10).\n- **Crash between spawn and record:** narrowed but not closed. The launch record is written right away when the child starts. A dashboard crash in that tiny window can still leave an untracked run; Scope notes explains how the operator handles it.\n- **Design mismatch:** the design says to add a line to a launch-prompt block in `formats.md`, but that file has no such block. The new line goes into the supervisor skill only (D7).\n- **Watcher gap:** I tested the file watcher (chokidar 3.6.0). It reports nothing for a file whose folder didn't exist when watching started, so the Overview watcher creates that folder first (D9).\n- **Evidence file:** besides the seven pending live-test lines, I added three lines for the plugin checks, which the last task marks passed once they run green (D11).\n- **Cut:** no fixture project ships; the operator makes a scratch one for the live tests.\n\nThere is no steering document in this repo, so the standards come from `agent-rules.md`.\n\nFiles are in `.spec-workflow/specs/harness-control-pane/`:\n- tasks.md\n- codebase-context.md (three new sections added at the end)","agentId":"a07373f8bd0fcabf4"}
